1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,746
Sam is replacing a legacy job that exports 40 accounts.

2
00:00:04,746 --> 00:00:10,033
Before switching, Sam has to show that the new export matches the old one.

3
00:00:10,033 --> 00:00:15,067
Veridelta pairs the rows by account ID and compares each column.

4
00:00:15,067 --> 00:00:18,541
39 rows differ, and one account is missing.

5
00:00:18,541 --> 00:00:24,167
In CI, exit code 1 fails the check. But is any of this a real error?

6
00:00:24,167 --> 00:00:29,033
Rules say which differences are expected, column by column.

7
00:00:29,033 --> 00:00:35,300
Veridelta cleans each side by those rules, then reports whatever they do not explain.

8
00:00:35,300 --> 00:00:38,390
Sam does not have to guess the rules.

9
00:00:38,390 --> 00:00:42,800
veridelta suggest tries each kind of rule on the columns that differ.

10
00:00:42,800 --> 00:00:48,267
It proposes three, each with the rows it explains, and calls no model.

11
00:00:48,267 --> 00:00:54,717
Sam adds a map from the old status words to the new letters. The rules live in one file.

12
00:00:54,717 --> 00:00:58,067
Now only two rows differ.

13
00:00:58,067 --> 00:01:05,045
Rules forgive rounding, case, empty markers, renamed codes, dates, and types.

14
00:01:05,045 --> 00:01:11,300
They cannot do arithmetic, like rounding to a multiple of seven, or compare two columns.

15
00:01:11,300 --> 00:01:16,814
Account 40 was closed on purpose, so a baseline file accepts it.

16
00:01:16,814 --> 00:01:20,420
The run accepts it, and one row still differs.

17
00:01:20,420 --> 00:01:24,433
So CI holds the rewrite until that row is fixed.

18
00:01:24,433 --> 00:01:30,691
The report shows that row side by side. Account 17 moved from south to east.

19
00:01:30,691 --> 00:01:34,267
That is the real error, out of 40 differences.

20
00:01:34,267 --> 00:01:38,509
Sam runs Veridelta in the terminal while writing the rules.

21
00:01:38,509 --> 00:01:45,067
Then the GitHub Action runs the same check on every pull request, and comments the result.

22
00:01:45,067 --> 00:01:52,533
Agents can call the same checks through MCP, and warehouse tables are compared where they are stored.

23
00:01:52,533 --> 00:01:56,679
Veridelta is early, and tested on generated data.

24
00:01:56,679 --> 00:01:58,933
Feedback is welcome.

25
00:01:58,933 --> 00:02:05,567
Try it with pip install veridelta.
